            <ArticleTitle>Selective synthesis of thioethers in the presence of a transition-metal-free solid Lewis acid.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2627-2635</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3762/bjoc.12.259</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The synthesis of thioethers starting from alcohols and thiols in the presence of amorphous solid acid catalysts is reported. A silica alumina catalyst with a very low content in alumina gave excellent results in terms of both activity and selectivity also under solvent-free conditions. The reaction rate follows the electron density of the carbinol atom in the substrate alcohol and yields up to 99% and can be obtained for a wide range of substrates under mild reaction conditions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
